## Trust boundaries
{{ range .Values.boundaries }}
- {{ . }}
{{- else }}
- Internet to edge: anything crossing it is hostile until proven otherwise.
- Service to datastore: credentials, network policy, least privilege.
- Operator to production: who can reach it, with what, and who sees that they did.
{{- end }}

## STRIDE

| Category | Threat | Mitigation | Status |
| -------- | ------ | ---------- | ------ |
{{- range .Values.threats }}
| {{ .category }} | {{ .threat }} | {{ .mitigation }} | {{ .status | default "open" }} |
{{- else }}
| Spoofing | Someone authenticates as another user | Per-request auth, short-lived tokens | open |
| Tampering | Payload modified between services | mTLS, signed messages | open |
| Repudiation | An action cannot be traced to an actor | Append-only audit log, clock sync | open |
| Information disclosure | Data read by the wrong party | Encryption at rest and in transit, scoped queries | open |
| Denial of service | The system is made unavailable | Rate limits, quotas, autoscaling with a ceiling | open |
| Elevation of privilege | A user gains rights they were not granted | Deny by default, review of every role change | open |
{{- end }}

